{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"4c59eb7c-f99e-432d-9769-cdb4ed161851","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Radians connect an angle to distance along a circle. Start with a circle of radius r, measured from its center.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Radians and arc length"},{"op":"diagram","id":"circle","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"ellipse","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":[0.32,0.32],"stroke":"solid"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.5,0.5],"label":"O"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.5,0.5],[0.82,0.5]],"stroke":"solid","label":"r"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"4c59eb7c-f99e-432d-9769-cdb4ed161851","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"4c59eb7c-f99e-432d-9769-cdb4ed161851","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The angle in radians is arc length divided by radius. Rearranging gives arc length equals radius times angle.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"radius2","canvas_id":"circle","from":[0.5,0.5],"to":[0.66,0.2229],"stroke":"solid"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"arc","canvas_id":"circle","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":0.32,"start_deg":-60,"end_deg":0,"stroke":"solid","label":"s"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"angle","canvas_id":"circle","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":0.1,"start_deg":-60,"end_deg":0,"stroke":"solid","label":"θ"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\theta=\\frac{s}{r}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad s=r\\theta"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the arc length equals the radius, how large is the angle in radians?","expected_gist":"One radian, because s divided by r equals one."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"4c59eb7c-f99e-432d-9769-cdb4ed161851","step":{"id":"s3","script":"For this sixty-degree sector, the angle is pi over three radians. With radius six centimeters, the arc measures two pi centimeters.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"given","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"r=6\\,\\mathrm{cm},\\qquad \\theta=60^\\circ=\\frac{\\pi}{3}"},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"given","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"s=6\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{3}=2\\pi\\,\\mathrm{cm}"},{"op":"point","id":"arcmark","canvas_id":"circle","at":[0.7771,0.34],"label":"2π cm"},{"op":"text","id":"reminder","anchor":{"el":"answer","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Use radians in the arc-length rule."}],"checkpoint":null}}
